From 4b652821dcbb74aaf8ca6440fbd56646424b5cd5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Vihan Aggarwal <mooimacow1234567@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 17:59:35 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 08/10] Mask builder: -P with an off-clock preflight, started
 at step 25; locked batch staging

From an advisor review:
- The builder ran under python -I, which drops PYTHONPATH: where the trainer's packages resolve only
  through it (or the tokenizer is not in tiktoken's cache), the child would fail and rank 0 would
  build the mask inline on the clock (+3-5 s). It now runs under -P (no script-directory imports,
  the environment kept), and a --check run before the clock (imports, tokenizer) raises if it cannot.
- The builder starts at step 25, still on the clock, once the loop is in steady state, so its CPU
  work does not compete with the host-bound first steps. wait() starts it if a run never got there.
- collect() drops the mapping instead of closing it, which raised BufferError if a view survived.
- PinnedBatchStaging.upload takes a lock: the loader thread (step 0's fetch, the val reads) shares
  the ring with the training loader.
- A/B README: warm caches for systems A/Bs; the GPU smoke test also times launches during a fresh
  pinned allocation, checks the val read reuses a training shard's block through close(), runs the
  threaded fetch with the GPU busy, and reports the builder's spawn-to-done time and THP.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
